      "message": "The previous code calculated the embolden level using `ft_matrix.xx` and `ft_matrix.xy`, which correctly accounted for any fake italic `skew` that was applied just above. The new `CFX_SubstFont::GetEmboldenLevelForRender` method uses the un-skewed `matrix.a` and `matrix.c` directly, so it will result in a smaller emboldening level when skew is applied.\\n\\nConsider modifying `GetEmboldenLevelForRender` to accept the pre-computed `ft_matrix.xx` and `ft_matrix.xy` (or just the sum of their absolute values) to maintain the original behavior.\\n\\nThere is also a subtle difference in overflow handling here: previously, if the `level` multiplication overflowed, `level.ValueOrDefault(0)` fell back to `0` and rendering continued safely without emboldening. Now, `checked_level.ValueOrDefault(-1)` returns `-1`, which causes `level \u003c 0` to be true and aborts the glyph rendering entirely by returning `nullptr`.",
